// family F5d (op evidence, s2 types.srs:675): an op whose signature has a {k: C} evidence binder needs C at the request site. In
// main (the root) an unprovided C is error[no-capability]; in any other unit it joins the unit's inferred row, so a caller without
// a handle for C fails with error[unhandled-effect]. A unit with its own evidence binder of C, or a handle for C before the
// request, provides it.
// prompt: the Datalog text of family F5d over the inputs sigG, evTy, reqOp, pcap, hat, mainU; output badNoCapM; adds row facts.
// prompt: also badLoopLen (error[length-unnamed], s2 neg array_loop): the length local of an Array.fill is bound inside a while
// body, so each run makes a new value and older arrays would get the new length.
// prompt: also badEscB (error[region-escape], s2 negs op_region_escape, op_result_escape_nested): a block that is not a def body
// ends with data (a data call or constructor without {..}, or an op with a Srs.Region binder) while a Region handle opened in that
// block before it closes at the block end, so the value outlives its region.
// prompt: also: an Array.fill result is data (it lives in the innermost Region handle, like a data call), and badPutEsc
// (error[region-escape], s2 neg array_put_str_escape): Array.put stores into an array of region x a value of a region y opened
// after x, so y dies first.
// prompt: also badSeal (error[cell-seal], s2 negs cell_seal_block, cell_seal_call): a Cell.put on cell w (directly, or through a
// callee that writes its param cell, paramW) while a Region handle x opened in the unit is still open, unless w was made in x or a
// younger region; the rule is by place: the value written is not tracked.
// prompt: also tp calls (s2 negs tparam_escape, tparam_escape_given; vic-m5r.15): a call of a def whose result is one of its []
// binders (input retTp, Gate.retTpText) may return an arg, or make the result from one through a given, so it is fresh data
// (dataRhs) when an arg is fresh data without {..}, and a returned tp call with a local arg lives where that local lives (lastIn).
def Gate.f5dRules(): Str = ".decl rawPtr(c1: number)\n.input rawPtr\n.decl opEv(c1: number, c2: number, c3: number)\n.decl opNeed(c1: number, c2: number, c3: number)\n.decl pcapK(c1: number, c2: number)\n.decl needK(c1: number, c2: number, c3: number)\n.decl covN(c1: number, c2: number, c3: number)\n.decl badNoCapM(c1: number)\n.output badNoCapM\n.decl badLoopLen(c1: number)\n.output badLoopLen\n.decl opData(c1: number, c2: number)\n.decl escData(c1: number, c2: number)\n.decl badEscB(c1: number)\n.output badEscB\n.decl badPutEsc(c1: number)\n.output badPutEsc\n.decl cellPutSym(c1: number)\n.input cellPutSym\n.decl cellNewSym(c1: number)\n.input cellNewSym\ndataRhs(u, r) :- cname(u, r, s), cellNewSym(s).\n.decl cellPutOn(c1: number, c2: number, c3: number)\n.decl paramW(c1: number, c2: number)\n.decl writeAt(c1: number, c2: number, c3: number)\n.decl youngCell(c1: number, c2: number, c3: number)\n.decl badSeal(c1: number)\n.output badSeal\ncellPutOn(u, w, j) :- cname(u, n, s), cellPutSym(s), ctok(u, n, j), argFirst(u, n, a, t), carg(u, n, w, k, t).\nparamW(v, k) :- cellPutOn(v, w, j), ppos(v, w, k).\nparamW(v, k) :- carg(v, n, w, k2, t), callee(v, n, g), paramW(g, k2), ppos(v, w, k).\nwriteAt(u, w, j) :- cellPutOn(u, w, j).\nwriteAt(u, w, j) :- carg(u, n, w, k, t), callee(u, n, g), paramW(g, k), ctok(u, n, j).\nyoungCell(u, w, x) :- alloc(u, w, y, p), regH(u, b, x), x <= y.\nbadSeal(u) :- writeAt(u, w, j), regH(u, b, x), x < j, bend(u, b, e), j < e, !youngCell(u, w, x).\ndataRhs(u, r) :- cname(u, r, s), fillSym(s).\nbadPutEsc(u) :- putSite(u, n), argFirst(u, n, a, t), carg(u, n, w, k, t), alloc(u, w, x, p), argLast(u, n, a2, t2), carg(u, n, v, k2, t2), alloc(u, v, y, q), x < y.\nopData(u, n) :- reqOp(u, c, o, j), ctok(u, n, j), opEv(c, o, k), regionCap(k).\nescData(u, r) :- dataRhs(u, r), !hasEv(u, r).\nescData(u, r) :- opData(u, r).\nbadEscB(u) :- lastE(u, r, b, j), !body(u, b), escData(u, r), regH(u, b, x), x < j.\nbadLoopLen(u) :- vb(u, m, v, b, r, p), cname(u, r, s), fillSym(s), argFirst(u, r, a, t), carg(u, r, nb, k, t), vb(u, m2, nb, b2, r2, q), loopb(u, ls, le), ls < q, q < le.\nopEv(c, o, k) :- sigG(c, o), evTy(c, x, k, a).\nopNeed(u, k, j) :- reqOp(u, c, o, j), opEv(c, o, k).\npcapK(u, k) :- pcap(u, x, k).\nneedK(u, k, j) :- opNeed(u, k, j), !pcapK(u, k).\n.decl allocSym(c1: number)\n.input allocSym\n.decl allocAt(c1: number, c2: number)\n.decl covA(c1: number, c2: number)\n.decl regionKnown(c1: number)\n.decl badNoRegion(c1: number)\n.output badNoRegion\nallocAt(u, j) :- cname(u, n, s), allocSym(s), ctok(u, n, j).\nregionKnown(0) :- regionCap(k).\ncovA(u, j) :- allocAt(u, j), regionCap(k), hat(u, k, h), h < j.\ncovA(u, j) :- allocAt(u, j), regionCap(k), pcapK(u, k).\nneedK(u, k, j) :- allocAt(u, j), regionCap(k), !pcapK(u, k).\nbadNoCapM(u) :- allocAt(u, j), mainU(u), !covA(u, j).\nbadNoRegion(u) :- allocAt(u, j), !mainU(u), !regionKnown(0).\ncovN(u, k, j) :- needK(u, k, j), hat(u, k, h), h < j.\nrow(u, k) :- needK(u, k, j), !mainU(u), !covN(u, k, j).\nbadNoCapM(u) :- needK(u, k, j), mainU(u), !covN(u, k, j).\n.decl retTp(c1: number)\n.input retTp\n.decl tpCall(c1: number, c2: number)\n.decl argIn(c1: number, c2: number, c3: number)\ntpCall(u, n) :- callee(u, n, v), retTp(v).\n.decl topVal(c1: number)\n.input topVal\n.decl impure(c1: number)\nimpure(v) :- hst(v, h, x, w, b).\nimpure(v) :- reqOp(v, c, o, j), !regionCap(c).\nimpure(v) :- opsite(v, n, x, o, j).\nimpure(v) :- callee(v, n, w), impure(w).\n.decl badCtHandle(c1: number)\n.output badCtHandle\nbadCtHandle(u) :- topVal(u), hst(u, h, x, w, b).\n.decl badImpure(c1: number)\n.output badImpure\nbadImpure(u) :- topVal(u), callee(u, n, v), impure(v).\n.decl badValEff(c1: number)\n.output badValEff\nbadValEff(u) :- topVal(u), reqOp(u, c, o, j), !regionCap(c).\n.decl badValRt(c1: number)\n.output badValRt\nbadValRt(u) :- ref(u, v), topVal(v), !topVal(u).\n.decl ptail(c1: number, c2: number, c3: number)\n.input ptail\n.decl caseFty(c1: number, c2: number, c3: number)\n.input caseFty\n.decl badEscP(c1: number)\n.output badEscP\nbadEscP(u) :- body(u, b), lastE(u, m, b, j), ee(u, m, e), evsite(u, e, x, t), regH(u, b, x), ptail(u, m, w), pbind(u, p, s, i, w), caseFty(s, i, ft), !nonPtrT(ft).\ntpCall(u, n) :- opsite(u, n, x, o, j), evTy(u, x, c, a), sigR(c, o, t), sigT(c, o, t).\nargIn(u, n, a) :- tpCall(u, n), argFirst(u, n, a, t).\nargIn(u, n, b) :- argIn(u, n, a), xe(u, a, b).\ndataRhs(u, n) :- tpCall(u, n), argIn(u, n, a), dataRhs(u, a), !hasEv(u, a).\nlastIn(u, y) :- body(u, b), lastE(u, r, b, j), tpCall(u, r), carg(u, r, w, k, t), alloc(u, w, y, p), p < t, !rebound(u, w, p, t).\n.decl atSym(c1: number)\n.input atSym\n.decl evX(c1: number, c2: number)\n.decl capX(c1: number, c2: number)\nevX(u, x) :- evTy(u, x, c, a).\ncapX(u, x) :- pcap(u, x, c).\ndataRhs(u, n) :- opsite(u, n, x, o, j), atSym(o), !evX(u, x), !capX(u, x).\n.decl csNew(c1: number, c2: number)\n.input csNew\ndataRhs(u, n) :- csNew(u, n).\n.decl hasDoneR(c1: number)\nhasDoneR(v) :- doneSym(d), sigR(v, d, r).\nbadAns(v) :- kOp(v, o), sigR(v, o, s), !hasDoneR(v), !sigT(v, o, s).\n.decl msReq(c1: number, c2: number)\nmsReq(u, n) :- reqOp(u, c, o, j), ctok(u, n, j), hfor(v, c), kOp(v, o).\nmsReq(u, n) :- opsite(u, n, x, o, j), hst(u, h, x, v, b), kOp(v, o).\n.decl msOk(c1: number, c2: number)\nmsOk(u, n) :- vb(u, m, w, b, n, p).\nmsOk(u, n) :- lastE(u, n, b, j).\n.decl badMsShape(c1: number)\n.output badMsShape\nbadMsShape(u) :- msReq(u, n), !msOk(u, n).\n.decl badMsState(c1: number)\n.output badMsState\nbadMsState(u) :- msReq(u, n), tsE(u, n, x, s), body(u, b), tsX(u, b, x, t), s != t.\n.decl provAt(c1: number, c2: number, c3: number)\nprovAt(u, n, c) :- need(u, n, c), pcap(u, x, c).\nprovAt(u, n, c) :- need(u, n, c), hst(u, h, x, w, b), hfor(w, c), h < n, n <= b.\nprovAt(u, n, c) :- need(u, n, c), hfor(u, h), regionCap(c).\nbadNoCap(u) :- need(u, n, c), !provAt(u, n, c).\n.decl ruleAtom(c1: number, c2: number, c3: number, c4: number, c5: number, c6: number, c7: number)\n.input ruleAtom\n.decl ruleLen(c1: number, c2: number, c3: number, c4: number)\n.input ruleLen\n.decl ruleBad(c1: number, c2: number)\n.input ruleBad\n.decl relU(c1: number, c2: number, c3: number, c4: number)\n.input relU\n.decl rstep(c1: number, c2: number, c3: number, c4: number, c5: number, c6: number)\n.decl ruleR(c1: number, c2: number, c3: number, c4: number)\n.decl ruleOf(c1: number, c2: number)\n.decl nextBound(c1: number, c2: number)\n.decl badRuleShape(c1: number)\n.output badRuleShape\n.decl badAmbFact(c1: number)\n.output badAmbFact\nrstep(c, r, cl, 0, s, s) :- ruleLen(c, r, cl, n), stateOf(c, s).\nrstep(c, r, cl, j, s, t) :- rstep(c, r, cl, i, s, m), ruleAtom(c, r, cl, i, j, 0, o), move(c, o, m, t).\nrstep(c, r, cl, j, s, t) :- rstep(c, r, cl, i, s, m), ruleAtom(c, r, cl, i, j, 1, q), ruleR(c, q, m, t).\nruleR(c, r, s, t) :- rstep(c, r, cl, n, s, t), ruleLen(c, r, cl, n).\nruleOf(c, r) :- ruleLen(c, r, cl, n).\nbadRuleShape(c) :- ruleBad(c, cl).\nbadRuleShape(c) :- ruleAtom(c, r, cl, i, j, 1, q), !ruleOf(c, q).\ntermOf(u, a) :- relU(u, r, a, b).\ntermOf(u, b) :- relU(u, r, a, b).\nnextBound(u, b) :- nextF(u, a, o, b).\nvOf(u, k, b, t) :- relU(u, r, a, b), vOf(u, k, a, s), capU(u, c), ruleR(c, r, s, t), !isState(u, b), !nextBound(u, b).\nunsat(u, k) :- cand(u, k), relU(u, r, a, b), !boundK(u, k, a).\nunsat(u, k) :- cand(u, k), relU(u, r, a, b), !boundK(u, k, b).\nunsat(u, k) :- cand(u, k), relU(u, r, a, b), vOf(u, k, a, s), vOf(u, k, b, t), capU(u, c), !ruleR(c, r, s, t).\n.decl ruleU(c1: number, c2: number)\nruleU(u, r) :- pcap(u, x, c), ruleOf(c, r).\nbadRel(u) :- relU(u, r, a, b), !ruleU(u, r).\nbadAmbFact(u) :- sol(u, k), vOf(u, k, b, t1), vOf(u, k, b, t2), t1 < t2.\n"
// prompt: (rules above) also the multi-shot checks (vic-hm63 C3 interim + Q-M4): msReq = an op node whose handler clause takes a continuation (kOp), qualified (reqOp) or on a handle binder (opsite); badMsShape (error[multishot-shape]) unless that node is a whole val rhs or a block's last expression; badMsState (error[multishot-state]) when a capability binder's state at such a node differs from its state at the end of the body; badAns (error[answer-type]) for a continuation clause of a handler without done whose result is no [] binder of the handler.

